04155007,-0.010397669859230518,-0.013232681900262833,0.011849642731249332,-0.010204469785094261,-0.006375736091285944,-0.013693167828023434,-0.00425668666139245,-0.011197937652468681,0.012034113518893719,0.007493047043681145,-0.003840323770418763,-0.027893515303730965,-0.012593474239110947,0.0053552002646028996,-0.0318332202732563,-0.00915404874831438,0.0138487434014678,0.012250878848135471,0.026670144870877266,0.031086133792996407,-0.02279593050479889,Automatic Directed CoT (AutoDiCoT),"Generating explanations for LLM reasoning, especially for incorrect labels, and using these to improve subsequent prompts.","During prompt engineering, when trying to understand why an LLM mislabels an item and how to correct its behavior.","An algorithm that automatically directs the Chain-of-Thought (CoT) process to reason in a particular way. For each development item, it labels it, then prompts the model to generate a reasoning chain. If the model labels incorrectly, it's prompted with 'It is actually [is/is not] entrapment, please explain why' to generate a corrective reasoning chain. These generated CoTs can then be used as exemplars (including 'bad reasoning' examples) in subsequent prompts.","Combines automatic CoT generation with showing examples of bad reasoning, leading to improved prompt performance and understanding of LLM behavior.","Prompt engineering, debugging LLM reasoning, automated exemplar generation for CoT.","Automatic Directed CoT, AutoDiCoT, Knowledge & Reasoning, LLM Reasoning, Explanation Generation, Prompt Engineering, Chain-of-Thought, CoT Prompting, Corrective Reasoning, Exemplar Generation, Bad Reasoning Examples, Prompt Improvement, Debugging LLM"
