24,0.00031950074480846524,0.021109605208039284,-0.0024407925084233284,-0.006888941861689091,-0.017542993649840355,0.007459990680217743,0.006026935297995806,6.0107031458755955e-05,0.0060966662131249905,-0.010698527097702026,-0.03955557569861412,-0.0142547357827425,0.016429107636213303,-0.025152679532766342,0.007950766012072563,0.0010602651163935661,0.006283059250563383,0.019249292090535164,0.03325965255498886,-0.024139469489455223,Exemplar Ordering,The order of exemplars in a few-shot prompt can significantly affect the LLM's behavior and accuracy.,"When designing few-shot prompts, especially for tasks where the model's performance is sensitive to the sequence of examples.","Carefully arrange the order of exemplars within the prompt. The text notes that 'randomly order exemplars' is a design decision, implying that *controlled* ordering (or even random ordering as a strategy) is a technique.","Can cause accuracy to vary significantly, implying that optimal ordering can lead to improved performance, while suboptimal ordering can degrade it.","Optimizing few-shot prompt performance, mitigating prompt sensitivity.","Exemplar Ordering, Prompt Design, Few-shot Prompt, LLM Behavior, Accuracy, Exemplar Selection, Prompt Sensitivity, Performance Optimization"
