9054363965988,0.008236382156610489,0.026228584349155426,-0.0001490304566686973,0.011813469231128693,0.004973670933395624,0.012941083870828152,0.011865098960697651,-0.0032113795168697834,-0.01345908734947443,-0.01855061948299408,-0.0003482403408270329,-0.030892346054315567,-0.0034107023384422064,-0.011782689020037651,-0.004076371435075998,0.011441151611506939,0.0445440337061882,0.03686189278960228,0.011551447212696075,-0.02261614054441452,Inherently Interpretable Models (Interpretability by Design),"High-performing machine learning models are often black-boxes, lacking transparency and interpretability, which is critical in high-stakes applications and can hinder trust and accountability.","Developing machine learning models for critical applications (healthcare, criminal justice, finance) where understanding the model's internal logic and decision-making process is paramount, and a perceived trade-off between accuracy and interpretability exists.","Design and train models that are intrinsically transparent and understandable to humans. This can involve using model architectures that are simple by nature (e.g., Decision Trees, Rule-based models, Linear Models, Generalized Additive Models, K-Nearest Neighbors, Naive Bayes) or by incorporating interpretability criteria directly into the model's optimization problem during training (e.g., minimizing model complexity like number of leaves or rules).","Models that provide direct insights into their decision-making process, fostering trust, enabling error analysis, and facilitating fairness assessment, often overcoming the perceived accuracy-interpretability tradeoff by optimizing for both.","Building trustworthy AI systems, satisfying regulatory requirements (e.g., GDPR), knowledge discovery, error analysis and debugging, fairness assessment, transferability, model comparison.","Inherently Interpretable Models, Interpretability by Design, Classical AI, Black-box Models, Transparency, Accountability, High-stakes Applications, Decision Trees, Rule-based Models, Linear Models, Generalized Additive Models, K-Nearest Neighbors, Naive Bayes, Trustworthy AI, Regulatory Requirements, Knowledge Discovery, Error Analysis, Debugging, Fairness Assessment, Transferability, Model Comparison"
