637377262,-0.0046045114286243916,-0.0008000707603059709,-0.014385366812348366,-0.0019231593469157815,0.0010664842557162046,-0.0027929716743528843,-0.0031908531673252583,0.002027517184615135,-0.02643897756934166,-0.01534764189273119,0.006694197189062834,-0.03024638444185257,0.012060879729688168,0.004450981970876455,0.01740190200507641,0.01239421870559454,0.03651444613933563,-0.02280670776963234,Open-Book Question Answering with InContext RALM,"Enabling frozen, pre-trained Language Models to answer open-domain questions accurately by leveraging external knowledge, without requiring fine-tuning or specific pre-training for QA.","A large, pre-trained LM (e.g., LLaMA) is available, but it lacks the specific knowledge or reasoning capabilities to answer open-domain questions reliably in a 'closed-book' setting. Fine-tuning is not desired or possible.","Extend the standard question-answering prompt by prepending relevant documents retrieved from a knowledge source (e.g., Wikipedia via DPR) to the LM's input. The LM then processes this augmented prompt (documents + question) to generate the answer. The number of documents can be optimized.","Significantly boosted performance in open-domain question answering tasks (e.g., exact match scores on NQ and TriviaQA) for frozen LMs, demonstrating their ability to leverage retrieved documents without further training.","Building robust open-domain question answering systems, improving factual accuracy in QA, leveraging general-purpose LMs for knowledge-intensive tasks.","Open-Book Question Answering, InContext RALM, AI-Human Interaction, Frozen Language Models, External Knowledge, Fine-tuning, Pre-trained LM, Open-domain Questions, Closed-book Setting, Relevant Documents, Knowledge Source, DPR, Augmented Prompt, NQ, TriviaQA, InContext Retrieval-Augmented Language Modeling, Retrieval-Augmented Generation, RAG, Factual Accuracy, Knowledge-intensive Tasks"
