57144270837307,0.02196158841252327,-0.0004289660428185016,-0.009168805554509163,-0.020010754466056824,-0.0019003646448254585,-0.0018746661953628063,0.006805080454796553,-0.0008247678633779287,-0.019354073330760002,-0.025515370070934296,-0.009725026786327362,-0.00749110197648406,-0.03646489232778549,0.001420957618393004,0.0031939400359988213,0.005766992922872305,0.015190028585493565,0.04356546700000763,-0.022424716502428055,Prompt-Tuning a Frozen LM as a Reader,"Adapting a pre-trained, frozen Language Model for a specific downstream task (e.g., Open-Domain Question Answering) without fine-tuning its weights, which can be costly or impossible.","A frozen LM is available, and it needs to perform a specific 'reading' task (like extracting answers from text or understanding a query) within a larger system (e.g., a RALM or QA system).","Instead of fine-tuning the LM's weights, design specific prompts or 'prompt-tunes' that guide the frozen LM to perform the desired task. This involves crafting the input text to elicit the correct behavior from the LM.","Enables frozen LMs to achieve competitive performance on downstream knowledge-intensive tasks like Open-Domain Question Answering, leveraging their pre-trained capabilities without expensive retraining.","Adapting LMs for QA, summarization, information extraction, or other specific tasks where fine-tuning is not an option.","Prompt-Tuning, Frozen LM, Reader, Prompt Design, Pre-trained Language Model, Downstream Task, Open-Domain Question Answering, QA, Fine-tuning, Prompt-tunes, Input Text Crafting, InContext Learning, InContext Retrieval-Augmented Language Modeling, Summarization, Information Extraction"
